Subject: [PATCH] =?UTF-8?q?dos:=20Phase=2010=20patch=200039=20=E2=80=94=20?=
 =?UTF-8?q?fix=20audio=5Firq=5Fwall=5Fus=20via=20RDTSC/PIT=20timer?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Bug: patch 0038 used BIOS tick at 0040:006C for IRQ entry/exit timing.
That was wrong: BIOS tick advances via IRQ-0 (timer interrupt), and
our audio IRQ-5 handler runs with CLI held by DPMI — IRQ-0 cannot
fire during our handler invocation. Result: entry_tick == exit_tick
ALWAYS, cumulative `doskutsu_audio_irq_wall_us` stayed 0 forever.
Iter 1 surfaced this; flush-instr's review accepted "cumulative-mean
converges" without sanity-checking the resolution-vs-rate ratio.

Fix: auto-detect a timer that advances independent of CLI:

  1. RDTSC (Pentium+, detected via CPUID): ~12 ns at PODP83's 83 MHz.
     Single-instruction read; advances per CPU cycle regardless of
     interrupt flag state. Calibrated cycles-per-µs at init via
     SDL_GetTicksNS as wall-clock reference.

  2. 8253 PIT counter 0 (always available; 486-class fallback):
     ~838 ns at 1.193 MHz. Latch+read via outportb(0x43,0x00) +
     two inportb(0x40) reads. IRQ-safe single-bus-cycle port I/O.
     16-bit wrap handled via modular subtraction (counter is
     always programmed at boot to mode 3 / 0xFFFF for IRQ-0).

  3. BIOS tick (kept as last-resort default if neither detected;
     known broken in IRQ context but harmless as it just gives 0
     deltas — same as pre-fix behavior).

CPUID detection via EFLAGS bit 21 flip-test (settable only on CPUs
that support CPUID; Pentium+ guaranteed, late-486DX4 may also have).
TSC support via CPUID(EAX=1) EDX bit 4.

Init banner logged at SDL_Log INFO level so DEBUG.LOG documents which
path was selected:
  "audio IRQ timer: RDTSC (Pentium-class detected, N cycles/us ~= N MHz)"
  "audio IRQ timer: 8253 PIT counter 0 (486-class fallback, ~838 ns/tick)"

SDL_DOSAudioInitTimer() called once from DOSSOUNDBLASTER_OpenDevice
BEFORE IRQ hook installs so first IRQ has correct mode set.

Inline timer-read helpers (SDL_DOSAudioReadTimer +
SDL_DOSAudioTimerDeltaUs) defined in SDL_dos_audio_synth.h so they
expand at the IRQ-handler call site — no external function call,
no memory-lock concerns. All underlying operations are IRQ-safe by
construction.

Per kbd-counter precedent (uint32_t volatile = atomic on x86):
g_dos_audio_timer_mode + g_dos_audio_timer_tsc_mhz are written
ONCE at init (non-IRQ context, before locking/hooking) and only
READ from IRQ context. Both DOS_LockVariable'd.

Smoke criteria:
  DOSBox-X: timer-mode banner emits cleanly (DOSBox-X simulates
  Pentium → RDTSC path); per-block irq_wall_us is non-zero.
  Real-HW (PODP83): same RDTSC path; per-block irq_wall_us
  ~7-70 ms aggregate (W20A2-equivalent ~13.5 ms/flip × ~5 flips/block).

ASCII-only log strings per dos_batch_files_crlf.md (no µ or ≈ chars
in DEBUG.LOG output; "us" + "~=" instead).

Out-of-scope for 0039: no idle-pause mechanism changes; no new env
vars; other counter conventions (irq_count, sfx_active_count, idle-
pause counters) unchanged.
